Pyro patch 0041: the window's prototype chain as WebIDL has it.

Patch 0004 put the named properties object right under the global: window -> WindowProperties ->
Object.prototype, with Window.prototype off to the side, and the global proxy fixed to that. WebIDL's
chain is window -> Window.prototype -> WindowProperties -> EventTarget.prototype -> Object.prototype,
which JavaScript cannot build (the global and the named properties object are immutable prototype
exotic objects). JSGlobalContextSetNamedPropertiesChain (JSForkPrivate.h) re-links it once the
embedder has made the interface prototype objects, keeping the global proxy: the global gets the new
prototype directly, and its proxy, retargeted to the same global, takes it into its structure
(resetPrototype would make a new proxy, which code already holding globalThis would not see).

The named properties object (patch 0004) now has WebIDL's internal methods besides [[GetOwnProperty]]:
[[DefineOwnProperty]], [[Delete]] and [[PreventExtensions]] fail (it stays extensible), and so does an
ordinary [[Set]] that would define a property on it, unless a setter further up the chain takes it
(`__proto__`). Script reaches the object under Window.prototype with Object.getPrototypeOf, where the
embedder's Proxy stand-in used to answer for it.

